<title>AUSTRALIA: Cricket-West Indies 183 for nine v Australia.</title>
<headline>Cricket-West Indies 183 for nine v Australia.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia were one wicket away from winning the second test after West Indies slumped to 183 for nine on the final day on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Kenneth Benjamin was caught by Mark Taylor at first slip for four from the bowling of Shane Warne.</p>
<p>Warne has 3-77 from 24 overs.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
